## Number Guessing Game Deluxe

### Difficulty Levels

```xiom
enum Difficulty {
  Easy;
  Medium;
  Hard;
}

fn difficulty_config(d: Difficulty) -> (Int, Int) {
  match d {
    Difficulty.Easy => (50, 10),
    Difficulty.Medium => (100, 7),
    Difficulty.Hard => (200, 5),
  }
}
```

### Game State with Structs

```xiom
type GameState {
  secret: Int;
  attempts: Int;
  max_attempts: Int;
  high_score: Int;
  hints_used: Int;
}
```

### Smart Hints

```xiom
fn give_hint(guess: Int, secret: Int, attempts: Int) -> Str {
  let diff = secret - guess;
  if diff < 0 { diff = -diff; };

  if diff == 0 { return "You got it!"; };
  if guess < secret { return "Too low!"; };
  if guess > secret { return "Too high!"; };

  if attempts == 3 && diff <= 5 { return "Very close! You're within 5."; };
  if attempts == 5 { return "Hint: The number is round."; };
  "Keep trying!"
}
```

### Scoring System

```xiom
fn calculate_score(attempts: Int, max_attempts: Int, difficulty: Difficulty) -> Int {
  let base = (max_attempts - attempts + 1) * 100;
  let multiplier = match difficulty {
    Difficulty.Easy => 1,
    Difficulty.Medium => 2,
    Difficulty.Hard => 3,
  };
  base * multiplier
}
```

### Leaderboard

```xiom
type Leaderboard {
  scores: Vec[Int];
}

fn add_score(lb: &mut Leaderboard, score: Int) {
  lb.scores.push(score);
  sort_descending(&mut lb.scores);
  if lb.scores.len() > 5 {
    lb.scores.remove(lb.scores.len() - 1);
  };
}
```

### Play Again Loop

```xiom
fn play_game() {
  let mut playing = true;
  let mut lb = Leaderboard{ scores: Vec[Int].new() };

  while playing {
    let score = play_round(Difficulty.Medium);
    add_score(&mut lb, score);
    io.println(score);

    io.println("Play again? (1=yes, 0=no)");
    let choice = 0;
    playing = choice == 1;
  };
}
```

